### Page 4 of 5

```text
Note 1: All bulky items including mattresses, couches, stoves, refrigerators, etc., will be collected and
charged by volume as an Extra Pickup.  The freon removal fee must be paid in addition to disposal fee for
all refrigerators, freezers, and air conditioners unless freon removal has been certified by a licensed
repairman.
Note 2: A “building,” for the purposes of Section 8.44.010 D of City Code, is defined as a non-residential
premises using a water meter.  Buildings will be assessed at least a “Basic Rate Fee” for each collection
point (i.e., container or set of containers) or charges based on the type and quantity of containers and
frequency of pickups as outlined in this Solid Waste Fee Schedule.  Multiple collocated, non-residential
buildings owned by a single property owner will be assessed at least a “Basic Rate Fee” equal to the number
of collection points.  If 1.5 Cubic Yard or larger city dumpsters are used, the Basic Rate Fee is included in
the fees for those containers.  Charges are normally included in water and sewer bills issued to property
owners or agents of such premises by the Board of Public Utilities.

Note 3: If material is left outside of dumpsters or if residents fail to control their waste, requiring manual
pickup, the owner of the property may be assessed this additional cleanup fee for manpower and equipment
time.

Note 4: City residents must show identification (driver’s license, etc.) and certify that material is their
personal household waste to receive reduced Transfer Station rates.

Note 5: Electronic Components: Charges to commercial entities for recycling of electronic components are
based on the City’s cost for recycling plus 10% for handling and processing. Contact the Solid Waste
Division for current prices.  Electronic components (computers, televisions, cell phones, etc.) contain
hazardous materials and must not be disposed of in the Landfill. Recycling of these components is free to
city/county residents at the Transfer Station.

Note 6: Tires larger than 20” will be charged by weight.

Note 7: Residents must present documentation from a doctor and certify that there is not an able-bodied
person living in the home to qualify for complimentary “Special Attention” services.  Documentation must
be updated on an annual basis to continue in the program. A sanitation division employee will move one
trash and one recycle auto cart from and return it to a designated and approved location each collection day.
Additional carts may be included if justification is provided, and an additional fee is paid.

Note 8: Residential recycle containers will be equal to or larger than residential trash containers.  To qualify
for the smaller 60-gallon recycle container, residents must also have a 60-gallon trash container.  Residents
may choose not to accept a recycle container; however, there will be no reduction in the residential
automated collection fee.

Note 9: Overweight or over-packed Roll-Off Containers will be charged double the disposal fee.
Overloaded cardboard containers will be charged based on time required to empty the container.

Note 10: Residential trash and recycle service may be suspended for full months only. Full month
suspension dates are based on billing cycles as defined by the Board of Public Utilities.

Note 11: The optional yard waste collection program may not be suspended, only discontinued. Residents
who pay for the optional yard waste container receive pickup of up to one cubic yard of limbs, tree
trimmings, hedge clippings and similar material.  Residents must cut items to less than three-foot lengths
and contact the Sanitation Division to schedule pickup.  Yard waste will be collected and charged by volume
as an Extra Pickup from customers who do not subscribe to the optional yard waste program.

Note 12: Place automated trash, recycle and yard waste containers a minimum of two feet from any object,
i.e., vehicles, trailers, fences, poles, trees, other containers, etc., and be sure the area in front of the container
(toward the street) is clear of obstructions. A Container Placement Fee is charged each time a driver must
exit the vehicle to move a container so it may be safely dumped without striking a nearby object. The fee
will not apply if a container is blown over by the wind or other act of nature.

Note 13:  These charges apply to customers who do not get a water bill.  Billing must be done manually by
Solid Waste Staff.

Note 14:  The Landfill Manager may request to inspect the origin of the soil and require testing to verify
the soil is uncontaminated.  Petroleum contaminated soil has minimum testing requirements per WDEQ
guidelines.  The customer will pay for any testing.  If requested, test results shall be provided to the Landfill
Manager a minimum of 48-hours prior to disposal.

Note 15:  The Public Works Director or Deputy Director may negotiate costs and terms for unusual requests
to dispose of material at the Landfill.  Examples include but are not limited to:  material from large
```

### Page 5 of 5

```text
commercial demolition or remodeling projects; material such as dirt that may be needed by the City; and
material from accidents or natural disasters.  Testing for hazardous materials may be required in these
instances.

Note 16: Waste containers and their contents placed within city limits in violation of city code Chapter
8.44, Solid Waste, will be removed and disposed of and an appropriate fee assessed to the owner. Fee will
be based on unscheduled contents disposal plus the Transfer Station disposal fee cost per ton.

Note 17: Contact the Sanitation Division to arrange waste collection for special events at least 10-business
days prior to the event. Special event waste collection arrangements made less that 10-business days prior
to the event will be subject to a 25% short notice fee. Orders under $300 are subject to a $50 administration
fee.

Note 18:  A fee equal to the “Unscheduled contents disposal for a 1.5 CY Container” will be charged when
Sanitation must return to service a blocked container, when a customer requests relocation of a container,
or when a container has been moved from its service location and requires relocation.
```
